# Rule 01. Block is the root of blocks and screens, Box is never a wrapper

Language-agnostic. Zones, `{kit}` and "component root" are defined in rule 00.

## Goal

The DOM tree follows HTML5 semantics strictly. Landmarks come only from
`Block`. Nested structure comes only from layout primitives.

## Rules

1. A file in the `blockRoot` part of the composition (blocks, app screens,
   page templates, the app frame) opens on `Block`, or on a composite whose own
   root is `Block` (a section frame). It never starts with `Box`, `Stack`,
   `Group`, `Grid`, `Card` or anything else.
2. Any other file (a composite component, a part, a screen part) may open on
   exactly one `Block` with a semantic tag (`nav`, `figure`, `article`,
   `header`, `footer`, `aside`, `section`, ...). Landmarks and sectioning
   elements come only from `Block`; there is no `Nav`, `Figure`, `Article`,
   `Header`, `Footer` or `Blockquote` primitive.
3. One file has at most one `Block`. The only exception is mutually exclusive
   branches of the same component: Svelte `{#if}` / `{:else if}` / `{:else}`,
   React ternary, `&&` / `||` alternatives and early returns, Vue `v-if` /
   `v-else-if` / `v-else`. Each branch may have its own single root-level
   `Block`, because only one of them renders. If a second `Block` is needed
   anywhere else (a sibling, after an `{#if}`, in another component or
   snippet of the same file), extract it into a separate file and import it.
4. `Block` is never nested inside another `Block` of the same file, and never
   repeated by a loop (`{#each}`, `.map`, `v-for`). If a nested or repeated
   region needs its own `Block`, move it into a new file and import that
   component. Composition across files is allowed. Nesting inside one file is
   not.
5. `Box` is never a wrapper and never a file root. It appears only where no
   specialised primitive fits: `Card`, `Stack`, `Group`, `Grid`, `List`,
   `Dialog` and the others found in `{kit}`.
6. `Box` is always a plain nested `div`. It is never a landmark and never
   imitates another primitive. ARIA (`role="group"`, `role="status"`, ...) goes
   through `Attrs`; Box has no role prop.
7. Before using `Box`, search `{kit}` for a primitive that expresses the
   intent. If the primitive is missing and the intent is repeatable, add it to
   the kit (its spec, for a generated kit) instead of piling up `Box`.

## Roots by surface

| Surface | Root |
| --- | --- |
| Application frame | `Block` without `tag`, a viewport container, not a landmark |
| Route, view or screen | `Block` with `tag=section` |
| Page header | `Block` with `tag=header` |
| Primary content | `Block` with `tag=main` and `id=main-content` |
| Complementary column | `Block` with `tag=aside` |

- `header` and `main` are siblings inside the application frame.
- There is exactly one `main` per page.
- The application frame never takes `tag=main`, `section` or `header`.

## Where to look for tags

1. Find the needed element in the primitives of `{kit}`.
2. If it is not there, check the tag groups in the utils of `{kit}`.
3. If it is still missing, extend the kit. Do not write a raw tag in the screen.

## Tag-to-primitive map (the codegen model)

| Primitive | Tags |
| --- | --- |
| `Block` | `div` (default), `section`, `article`, `aside`, `header`, `footer`, `main`, `nav`, `figure`, `search`, `hgroup`; props `ID`, `Class`, `Tag`, `Attrs`, `Children` |
| `Box` | `div` only |
| `Container` | `div`, `main`, `section` |
| `Stack` | `div`, `ul`, `ol` |
| `Group` | `div`, `fieldset`, `dl` |
| `List` / `ListItem` | `ul`, `ol`, `dl`, `menu` / `li`, `dt`, `dd` |
| `Title` | `h1` to `h6` (`As` 1 to 6) |
| `Text` | `p` (default), `blockquote`, `figcaption`, `address`, `pre`, and the inline elements (`span`, `strong`, `em`, ...) |
| `Inline` | `span` |

ARIA goes through `Attrs`. Inside phrasing content (a button, a label, a
summary) use `Inline` or `Text` with an inline tag, never `Stack` or `Group`.

## Nested replacements

- A nested navigation, figure, article, header or footer (inside a card, a
  block or a loop item) comes from a separate file rooted on `Block` with that
  tag (generator: `NavBlock`, `FigureBlock`, `ArticleBlock`), never a nested
  `Block` in the same file.
- A quotation is `Text tag="blockquote"`; a caption is `Text tag="figcaption"`.
- A centered modal is `Dialog`, never `Block` plus a dialog role.
- A grid is `Grid`, never `Box` with grid classes.

## How the generator keeps one Block per file

- **Screens.** A screen opens on `Block tag="main" id="main-content"`, exactly one per page.
  Gallery and catalog pages wrap their content in a page section
  (`Block tag="section" aria-labelledby="page-title"`, the first level-1 `Title` gets
  `id="page-title"`). Theme sections inside a page are labelled groups (`Stack role="group"`).
- **Screen parts.** Chrome that needs its own landmark (the screen header with the skip
  link inside it) is emitted as a separate file, a screen *part* (`part("ScreenHeader")`),
  so every file still has one `Block` per render path.
- **Frames.** Organisms marked `frame: true` (section frame, region, hero head, sidebar
  panel, shell top bar / sidebar / footer, help and footer cards) are checked as block files:
  they must open on `Block` (the `blockRoot` zone), never nested.
- **Composites.** A composite opens on `Box` (role="group" through attrs for a panel) or
  on one `Block` with a semantic tag. A `nav`, `figure` or `article` nested inside a block
  root or repeated in a loop is the part `NavBlock` / `FigureBlock` / `ArticleBlock`
  (`xgen/screens/src/authoring/components/landmarks.ts`): its own file, rooted on
  `Block`, so the parent file still holds one Block and none in a loop.
- **Cards** that are whole blocks (pricing, product, post) open on `Block tag="article"`
  with the card classes (`cardBase()`) and `data-slot="card"`.
- **Backdrops.** `Backdrop` / `OverMedia` are only a picture layer
  (`absolute inset-0 -z-10`) placed inside the block root, which `behind()` makes
  `relative isolate overflow-hidden`; they never wrap the block. Before, the wrapper sat outside the section and the section background covered the picture (it never showed); now the faint picture is visible as designed (deliberate change, hero "over a picture" demo and theme events hero).

## Validation

`bun run check`, group `rules`, detector `block-root`, fails when:

- the first rendered node of a `blockRoot` file is not `Block` (directly or through a composite whose root is `Block`);
- a render path of the file holds more than one `Block`: exclusive branches are
  alternatives (a path takes one of them), everything else adds up, including
  detached markup such as a second component or a snippet;
- `Block` is nested inside another `Block` of the same file;
- `Block` sits inside a loop (`{#each}`, `.map` / `.flatMap` / `Array.from`, `v-for`).

Fixtures per runtime: `rules/fixtures/<runtime>/block-root.{branches.ok,siblings.bad,nested.bad,loop.bad}`.

Not checked by the tool yet (review): `Box` used as a wrapper, the landmark
`tag` of the application frame, one `main` per page.
